# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore
#
# One thing to know before editing this file: this project is a disk cleaner,
# so its test fixtures are deliberately named like the junk it removes —
# tmp/, .cache/, *.log, .Trash/. A normal, unanchored junk rule therefore makes
# the test suite's own fixtures silently uncommittable.
#
# Two conventions keep that from happening:
#   * directory rules are anchored to the repository root with a leading "/",
#     because git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded;
#   * file rules are left unanchored but exempted under tests/fixtures/ by the
#     negation at the bottom, which does work for files.
#
# If you add a rule here, run:  git check-ignore -v <a representative path>
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# macOS metadata
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.fseventsd
.Spotlight-V100
.TemporaryItems
.Trashes
.VolumeIcon.icns
.com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent

docs/info.txt

# Editors and IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/
.vs/
.zed/
*.swp
*.swo
*.swm
*~

# Local environment and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template

# Logs, process files, and temporary artifacts
*.log
*.pid
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
/tmp/
/temp/

# Local tool caches
/.cache/

# The tool's own output, if anyone ever points HOME at a checkout while
# testing by hand rather than through ./tests/run. The cleanmymac paths are
# the tool's previous name, kept so an older checkout stays clean.
/Library/
/.config/mimi/
/.config/cleanmymac/
/.Trash/

# Scratch files from one-off tooling; never part of a change.
/scratch_*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test fixtures are never ignored.
#
# tests/fixtures/ holds deliberately junk-shaped trees (a fake ~/.cache, stray
# *.log files, a tmp/ directory) that the suite needs committed. This negation
# re-includes them from the file rules above; the directory rules above are
# root-anchored so they never match in here to begin with.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!tests/fixtures/**
